fund-js/12-event-loop-and-promises/01-wi.solution:
export function withTimeout(promise, ms) {
  let timer;
  const timeout = new Promise((_, reject) => {
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
      const err = new Error(`timed out after ${ms}ms`);
      err.name = 'TimeoutError';
      reject(err);
    }, ms);
  });
  return Promise.race([promise, timeout]).finally(() => clearTimeout(timer));
}

fund-js/12-event-loop-and-promises/01-wi.explanation:
`Promise.race` settles with whichever promise settles first; `finally` runs either way and clears the timer:

```js
let timer;
const timeout = new Promise((_, reject) => {
  timer = setTimeout(() => {
    const err = new Error(`timed out after ${ms}ms`);
    err.name = 'TimeoutError';
    reject(err);
  }, ms);
});
return Promise.race([promise, timeout]).finally(() => clearTimeout(timer));
```

Without the `clearTimeout`, a server making thousands of fast calls keeps thousands of pointless timers alive (and a short script cannot exit until they fire).
